  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The air in a room is heated using spherical heaters. Heater A has radius <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span>, temperature <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"T\"></span> and an emissivity of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.50\"></span>. Heater B has a radius of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R}{4}\"></span>, a temperature of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4T\"></span> and an emissivity of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.75\"></span>. It takes Heater A one minute to raise the temperature of the room by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1\"></span> K. How long does it take for Heater B to raise the temperature of the room by <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span> K?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"5.0\"></span> s</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"20\"></span> s</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"80\"></span> s</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"320\"></span> s</li>\n</ol>"
  },
